        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 id="spray-force">Spray Force and Atomization Physics</h2>
            <p>Spray force in an aerosol system originates from a <strong>pressure differential</strong> between the can
                interior and ambient atmosphere. This pressure drop accelerates the formulation through the valve
                orifice, creating shear forces that break the liquid into droplets. Atomization quality depends on
                pressure magnitude, flow velocity, and fluid properties.</p>
            <p>Propellants influence atomization not by chemistry alone, but by how consistently they maintain pressure
                during discharge. Higher and more stable pressure produces finer droplets and more uniform spray
                patterns.</p>
