        <section>
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
            <p><strong>Can the same formulation behave differently with different propellants?</strong><br>Yes. Changes
                in vapor pressure, solvency, and discharge behavior directly affect spray force and stability even if
                the formulation remains unchanged.</p>
            <p><strong>Why do compressed gas aerosols feel weak near end-of-can?</strong><br>Compressed gases lose
                pressure continuously during discharge because no liquid phase exists to replenish vapor pressure.</p>
            <p><strong>Is DME suitable for all aerosol products?</strong><br>No. While DME offers solvency benefits, it
                requires careful material compatibility evaluation due to seal and coating interactions.</p>
            <p><strong>Does climate affect propellant performance?</strong><br>Yes. Temperature strongly influences
                vapor pressure, making climate a critical factor in propellant selection, especially in India.</p>
        </section>

